<title>USA: Telechips delisted by Nasdaq, cuts jobs.</title>
<headline>Telechips delisted by Nasdaq, cuts jobs.</headline>
<dateline>RENO, Nev. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telechips Corp on Tuesday said the Nasdaq Small Capitalization Market delisted its stock because the company was unable to meet the exchange's listing requirements.</p>
<p>The company said its shares would be available immediately for trading through the NASD Bulletin Board.</p>
<p>Telechips said that it has experienced delays in completing financing, and that it has been forced to lay off all its employees.</p>
<p>The company sells Windows-compatible client computing and communications devices.</p>
</text>
